{"total_count":1,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17/events","html_url":"https://github.com/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17","id":3649523498,"node_id":"I_kwDOP2kKL87Zh08q","number":17,"title":"Safety issue trigger from \"winning-avg-corewars\" test with OpenAI","user":{"login":"dopper","id":1493629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTM2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1493629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper","html_url":"https://github.com/dopper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dopper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-20T23:13:06Z","updated_at":"2025-11-20T23:13:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Cross posting from https://github.com/laude-institute/terminal-bench/issues/1361 \n\nHi Team,\ntl;dr implement safety message with OpenAI (https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/safety-best-practices) to not trigger warnings on api call. I have a working version that works for my test at the end if you want to review as a potential PR or just integrate directly.\n\nI have been running through the terminal bench runs and have run into some safety triggers with OpenAI getting emails on trigger words. Here is a report with the findings and potential solution:\n\nHarbor Terminal Bench — Safety Findings (2025-11-20)\n\nScope (self-contained)\n\nBench task: Core Wars “winning average” challenge located under jobs/[agent-model]/winning-avg-corewars__ucKkzu9.\nContext: Prompts and logs use “bomber”/“DAT bombs” terminology. Even though this is a simulation, the strings mirror weapon language and can trip OpenAI safety checks.\nEvidence (quoted so reviewers don’t need repo access)\n\nPrompt file jobs/[agent-model]/winning-avg-corewars__ucKkzu9/agent/command-1/command.txt\n“…stone.red - Classic stone bomber that drops DAT every 4 positions”\n“…g2-clear.red - G2-Clear that wipes memory with deadly DAT bombs”\nExecution log jobs/[agent-model]/winning-avg-corewars__ucKkzu9/agent/command-1/stdout.txt\nWhile printing warriors/stone.red: “Strategy Classic stone bomber - drops DAT every 4 positions”\nWhile printing warriors/g2-clear.red: “Strategy Simple clear loop… (includes bomb label and double mov of bomb payload)”\nSession trace jobs/[agent-model]/winning-avg-corewars__ucKkzu9/agent/sessions/2025/11/20/rollout-2025-11-20T09-47-17-019aa0a9-3e12-77e2-8a1a-aeb5d040acfe.jsonl\nTool-call logs and reasoning repeatedly include tokens: “bomber”, “bomb”, “bombing”, “bombs”, e.g., entries describing “stone bomber”, “DAT bombs”, “bombing routine”.\nRisk\n\nAlthough the content is about a simulation, repeated “bomb”/“bomber” strings may be flagged by OpenAI safety systems as weapon-related.\nCurrent requests to the API in this bench flow do not pass an explicit safety_identifier, reducing traceability and hampering automated policy routing.\nRecommended Action (PR-ready)\n\nPlumb safety_identifier=\"user_123456\" (use env var and convert to hash) into all Harbor terminal bench API calls (per OpenAI guidance: https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/safety-best-practices and https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/safety-checks).\nAdd a pre-dispatch guard: scan outgoing prompts for weapon-like tokens (bomb, bomber, explosive, etc.). If present, enforce the safety identifier before sending.\nAdd a regression test using this Core Wars prompt text to ensure prompts containing simulated “bomb/bomber” wording still execute with the safety identifier attached and are not blocked.\nDocument the behavior in bench README/runbook so future tasks with game-theoretic “bomb” language remain compliant.\nDesired Outcome (definition of done)\n\nCode: safety identifier wired into the bench submission path; guard enabled on weapon-like tokens.\nTests: regression covering the quoted Core Wars prompt; CI asserts the identifier is present when weapon-like terms appear.\nDocs: brief note in Harbor bench README/runbook on the safety identifier requirement for prompts containing game/simulated weapon terms.\nMy solution:\nsrc/harbor/llms/lite_llm.py\nText Compare\nProduced: 11/20/25 10:22:17 AM\n\n-+ 3 import os\n\n-+ 233 # Add safety_identifier for OpenAI models to indicate benchmark testing\n234 # Per OpenAI documentation: https://help.openai.com/en/articles/5428082\n235 # The identifier should be a hash of the username or email\n236\n237 # Check if this is an OpenAI model using comprehensive detection\n238 # This covers all OpenAI models including GPT, O1, embeddings, legacy, etc.\n239 model_lower = self.model_name.lower()\n240 is_openai_model = (\n241 # Explicit OpenAI indicator\n242 \"openai\" in model_lower or\n243 # Check for OpenAI model prefixes (most comprehensive)\n244 model_lower.startswith((\n245 \"gpt-\", # GPT-3.5, GPT-4, GPT-4o models\n246 \"o1-\", # O1 series models\n247 \"o1\", # O1 base model\n248 \"text-embedding-\", # Embedding models\n249 \"dall-e-\", # Image generation\n250 \"whisper-\", # Speech-to-text\n251 \"tts-\", # Text-to-speech\n252 \"text-davinci-\", # Legacy models\n253 \"text-curie-\", # Legacy models\n254 \"text-babbage-\", # Legacy models\n255 \"text-ada-\", # Legacy models\n256 \"davinci-\", # Legacy models\n257 \"curie-\", # Legacy models\n258 \"babbage-\", # Legacy models\n259 \"ada-\", # Legacy models\n260 )) or\n261 # Additional keyword checks for custom/future models\n262 any(keyword in model_lower for keyword in [\"gpt\", \"turbo\", \"davinci\"])\n263 )\n264\n265 if is_openai_model:\n266 # Get user identifier from environment\n267 # Priority: HARBOR_USER_ID > OPENAI_USER_EMAIL > USER > default\n268 user_identifier = (\n269 os.environ.get(\"HARBOR_USER_ID\") or\n270 os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_USER_EMAIL\") or\n271 os.environ.get(\"USER\") or\n272 \"harbor_default_user\"\n273 )\n274\n275 # Create SHA256 hash of the user identifier\n276 # Use only first 12 chars of hex digest for brevity\n277 user_hash = hashlib.sha256(user_identifier.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n278\n279 # Format as per OpenAI requirements: \"user\"\n280 completion_kwargs.setdefault(\"extra_body\", {})[\"safety_identifier\"] = (\n281 f\"user_{user_hash}\"\n282 )\n283","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/harbor-framework/terminal-bench-2/issues/17/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}